sues/117294","id":4037468159,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wpt__","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-11T08:40:20Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T08:41:56Z","body":"What behavior does this show with integer textures? If it matches how Vulkan looks, then it should be ok.\r\n\r\nGiven this function takes a \"Color\", it doesn't seem like it was intended to be used for integer textures in the first place.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4037468159/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4042361726","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117294#issuecomment-4042361726","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117294","id":4042361726,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7w8Yt-","user":{"login":"H3x4g0n","id":39725802,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NzI1ODAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39725802?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n","html_url":"https://github.com/H3x4g0n","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-11T21:33:54Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T21:33:54Z","body":"The behavior with integer textures is very inconsistent and seems to depend on how the underlying graphics driver implements the Vulkan/D3D12 API. I tested this today with different `UINT16` texture formats on a dedicated AMD GPU (RX 5700 XT) and integrated graphics from Intel.\r\n\r\n**Before:**\r\n| `DataFormat` | Vulkan (Intel) | Vulkan (AMD) | D3D12 (Intel) |  D3D12 (AMD) |\r\n| :---: | ------------- | ------------- | ------------- | ------------- |\r\n| `R16_UINT` | `R: 65535` | `R: 0` | `R: 255` | `R: 255` |\r\n| `R16G16_UINT`  | `R: 65535`<br>`G: 65535` | `R: 0`<br>`G: 53971` | `R: 255`<br>`G: 105`  | `R: 255`<br>`G: 105` |\r\n| `R16G16B16A16_UINT`  | `R: 65535`<br>`G: 65535`<br>`B: 65535`<br>`A: 65535` | `R: 0`<br>`G: 53971`<br>`B: 46261`<br>`A: 0` | `R: 255`<br>`G: 105`<br>`B: 180`<br>`A: 255` | `R: 255`<br>`G: 105`<br>`B: 180`<br>`A: 255` |\r\n\r\n**This PR:**\r\n| `DataFormat` | Vulkan (Intel) | Vulkan (AMD) | D3D12 (Intel) |  D3D12 (AMD) |\r\n| :---: | ------------- | ------------- | ------------- | ------------- |\r\n| `R16_UINT` | `R: 65535` | `R: 0` | `R: 65535` | `R: 1` |\r\n| `R16G16_UINT`  | `R: 65535`<br>`G: 65535` | `R: 0`<br>`G: 53971` | `R: 65535`<br>`G: 65535`  | `R: 1`<br>`G: 0` |\r\n| `R16G16B16A16_UINT`  | `R: 65535`<br>`G: 65535`<br>`B: 65535`<br>`A: 65535` | `R: 0`<br>`G: 53971`<br>`B: 46261`<br>`A: 0` | `R: 1`<br>`G: 0`<br>`B: 0`<br>`A: 1` | `R: 1`<br>`G: 0`<br>`B: 0`<br>`A: 1` |\r\n\r\n_Main conclusion:_ Clearing integer textures using `RenderingDevice::texture_clear()` is not consistent between the Vulkan and D3D12 driver, neither before nor with this PR - the inconsistency is just different. Mainly that, before this PR, clearing integer textures with the D3D12 driver was at least consistent when using different hardware. This somewhat makes sense, when considering that `ClearUnorderedAccessViewFloat()` was reported to handle data type conversions differently, depending on the GPU vendor.\r\n\r\nIn my opinion, `RenderingDeviceDriver::command_clear_color_texture()` should always use the respective float clearing function of the underlying graphics API, since the clear color is supplied as floats to `RenderingDevice::texture_clear()`.\r\n\r\nFurthermore, clearing integer textures with `RenderingDevice::texture_clear()` seems like a bad idea and I think that ultimately there should be a separate clearing function for integer textures.\r\n\r\n_On a note:_ before this PR, setting `TEXTURE_USAGE_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BIT` also leads to the expected clearing behavior of float textures when using D3D12. However, clearing with the Vulkan driver leads to the same result with and without setting `TEXTURE_USAGE_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BIT`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4042361726/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4047100646","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117294#issuecomment-4047100646","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117294","id":4047100646,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7xOdrm","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-12T14:13:55Z","updated_at":"2026-03-12T14:13:55Z","body":"Thanks! Congratulations on your first merged contribution! 🎉 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4047100646/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]